<title>GERMANY: DB Research cuts Thyssen to neutral.</title>
<headline>DB Research cuts Thyssen to neutral.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>DB Research, the research wing of Deutsche Bank AG said on Friday it had downgraded the industrial stocks Thyssen and Krupp-Hoesch to neutral from overweight.  </p>
<p>DB Research cut its earnings per share forecasts for Thyssen for 1996 to 14 marks from 17 marks, to 20 marks from 25 marks for 1997 and to 28 marks from 29 marks for 1998.</p>
<p>DB Research said that it had made the downgrades and the EPS outlook cuts because of disappointing price performance in the stainless steel and carbon steel sectors.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
